{
  "id": "minimum-window-substring",
  "questionId": "minimum-window-substring",
  "slug": "minimum-window-substring",
  "title": "Minimum Window Substring",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "category": "Sliding window",
  "patterns": [
    "sliding window",
    "variable-size window"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "blind-75",
    "grind-75",
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "this is the same grow-then-shrink shape as Minimum Size Subarray Sum, but 'valid' now means something more complex than a sum. how would you check validity here without rescanning the whole window every time?",
    "build a frequency count of what t requires; as you grow the window to the right, track how many of those requirements are currently satisfied",
    "once every requirement is satisfied, the window is valid - try shrinking from the left one character at a time, updating your satisfied-count, and record the window if it's still valid and shorter than your best so far",
    "stop shrinking the moment removing the left character would break a requirement, then go back to growing the right edge"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "recomputing whether the window is valid from scratch after every single character move, instead of tracking a running count of satisfied requirements",
    "not handling duplicate characters in t correctly (needing 2 of a character means having only 1 doesn't satisfy that requirement)",
    "shrinking past the point of validity, or forgetting to record the best window before continuing to shrink"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two strings, `s` and `t`.\n\n**Find the shortest substring of `s` that contains every character of `t`, and return it, or an empty string if no such substring exists.**\n\nMatching means duplicate counts too: if `t` has two 'a's, the substring must have at least two 'a's as well.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= s.length <= 10^5",
      "0 <= t.length <= 10^5",
      "s and t consist of uppercase and lowercase English letters"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "t is longer than s (always impossible)",
      "t requires more of a character than s contains in total",
      "s already equals t"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"ADOBECODEBANC\", t = \"ABC\"",
        "output": "\"BANC\"",
        "expectedOutput": "\"BANC\"",
        "explanation": "\"BANC\" is the shortest substring of s containing an A, a B, and a C"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"a\", t = \"a\"",
        "output": "\"a\"",
        "expectedOutput": "\"a\"",
        "explanation": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"a\", t = \"aa\"",
        "output": "\"\"",
        "expectedOutput": "\"\"",
        "explanation": "t needs two a's, but s only has one, so no valid window exists"
      }
    ],
